# Line endings are pinned rather than left to the machine's core.autocrlf,
# because two files here actually care:
#
#  - *.bat must be CRLF. cmd.exe misparses an LF-only batch file (a REM line
#    turns into an unknown command), which is how stop.bat first failed.
#  - everything else is LF, so a checkout on another machine doesn't rewrite
#    source and produce a diff that is nothing but line endings.
#
# Nothing here affects the save codec: it reads bytes off disk with its own
# latin1 handling and never goes through git.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf

# Reference data shipped with the app - normalising these gains nothing and a
# whitespace-only rewrite would obscure real changes.
webapp/data/*.json -text
